#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:61
msgid "Lumped model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:63
msgid ""
"The lumped thermal model solves the following ordinary differential equation "
"for the average temperature, given here in dimensional terms,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:65
msgid ""
"\\rho_{eff} \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t} = \\bar{Q} - \\frac{hA}{V}(T-"
"T_{\\infty}),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:70
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\rho_{eff}` is effective volumetric heat capacity, :math:`T` "
"is the temperature, :math:`t` is time, :math:`\\bar{Q}` is the averaged heat "
"source term, :math:`h` is the heat transfer coefficient, :math:`A` is the "
"surface area (available for cooling), :math:`V` is the cell volume, and :"
"math:`T_{\\infty}` is the ambient temperature. An initial temperature :math:"
"`T_0` must be prescribed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:72
msgid "The effective volumetric heat capacity is computed as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:74
msgid "\\rho_{eff} = \\frac{\\sum_k \\rho_k c_{p,k} L_k}{\\sum_k L_k},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:79
msgid ""
"where :math:`\\rho_k` is the density, :math:`c_{p,k}` is the specific heat, "
"and :math:`L_k` is the thickness of each component. The subscript :math:`k "
"\\in \\{cn, n, s, p, cp\\}` is used to refer to the components negative "
"current collector, negative electrode, separator, positive electrode, and "
"positive current collector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:81
msgid ""
"The heat source term accounts for Ohmic heating :math:`Q_{Ohm,k}` due to "
"resistance in the solid and electrolyte, irreverisble heating due to "
"electrochemical reactions :math:`Q_{rxn,k}`, reversible heating due to "
"entropic changes in the the electrode :math:`Q_{rev,k}`, and heating due to "
"contact resistance :math:`Q_{cr}`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:83
msgid "Q = Q_{Ohm,k}+Q_{rxn,k}+Q_{rev,k}+Q_{cr},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:88
msgid "with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:90
msgid ""
"Q_{Ohm,k} = -i_k \\nabla \\phi_k, \\quad Q_{rxn,k} = a_k j_k \\eta_k, \\quad "
"Q_{rev,k} = a_k j_k T_k \\frac{\\partial U}{\\partial T} \\bigg|"
"_{T=T_{\\infty}}, Q_{cr} = \\frac{R_{cr}}{V_{cell}}i_k^2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:95
msgid ""
"Here :math:`i_k` is the current, :math:`\\phi_k` the potential, :math:`a_k` "
"the surface area to volume ratio, :math:`j_k` the interfacial current "
"density, :math:`\\eta_k` the overpotential, :math:`U` the open-circuit "
"potential, :math:`R_{cr}` is the contact resistance, and :math:`V_{cell}` is "
"the total cell volume. The averaged heat source term :math:`\\bar{Q}` is "
"computed by taking the volume-average of :math:`Q`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:106
msgid ""
"When using the option ``{\"cell geometry\": \"arbitrary\"}`` the relevant "
"parameters to specify the cooling conditions are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:108
msgid "\"Total heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:109
msgid "\"Cell cooling surface area [m2]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:110
msgid "\"Cell volume [m3]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:112
msgid ""
"which correspond directly to the parameters :math:`h`, :math:`A` and :math:"
"`V` in the governing equation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:114
msgid ""
"When using the option ``{\"cell geometry\": \"pouch\"}`` the parameter :math:"
"`A` and :math:`V` are computed automatically from the pouch dimensions, "
"assuming a single-layer pouch cell, i.e. :math:`A` is the total surface area "
"of a single-layer pouch cell and :math:`V` is the volume. The parameter :"
"math:`h` is still set by the \"Total heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\" "
"parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:116
msgid ""
"When using the option ``{\"contact resistance\": \"true\"}`` the parameter "
"\"Contact resistance [Ohm]\" must be specified to calculate the heating from "
"contact resistance, which corresponds to :math:`R_{cr}`. \"Cell volume "
"[m3]\" is :math:`V_{cell}` within the governing equation. The default lumped "
"model option is ``{\"contact resistance\": \"false\"}``."
msgstr ""

