#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:260
msgid "Pouch cell models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:272
msgid "1D (through-cell) model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:274
msgid ""
"The 1D model solves for :math:`T(x,t)`, capturing variations through the "
"thickness of the cell, but ignoring variations in the other dimensions. The "
"temperature is found as the solution of a partial differential equation, "
"given here in dimensional terms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:276
msgid ""
"\\rho_k c_{p,k} \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t} = \\lambda_k \\nabla^2 T + "
"Q(x,t) - Q_{cool}(x,t)\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:278
msgid "with boundary conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:280
msgid ""
"-\\lambda_{cn} \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial x}\\bigg|_{x=0} = h_{cn}"
"(T_{\\infty} - T) \\quad -\\lambda_{cp} \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial "
"x}\\bigg|_{x=1} = h_{cp}(T-T_{\\infty}),\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:282
msgid "and initial condition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:284
msgid ""
"T\\big|_{t=0} = T_0.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:286
msgid ""
"Here :math:`\\lambda_k` is the thermal conductivity of component :math:`k`, "
"and the heat transfer coefficients :math:`h_{cn}` and :math:`h_{cp}` "
"correspond to heat transfer at the large surface of the pouch on the side of "
"the negative current collector, heat transfer at the large surface of the "
"pouch on the side of the positive current collector, respectively. The heat "
"source term :math:`Q` is as described in the section on lumped models. The "
"term :math:`Q_cool` accounts for additional heat losses due to heat transfer "
"at the sides of the pouch, as well as the tabs. This term is computed "
"automatically by PyBaMM based on the cell geometry and heat transfer "
"coefficients on the edges and tabs of the cell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:289
#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:355
msgid ""
"The relevant heat transfer parameters are: \"Negative current collector "
"surface heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\" \"Positive current collector "
"surface heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\" \"Negative tab heat transfer "
"coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\" \"Positive tab heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2."
"K-1]\" \"Edge heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:291
msgid ""
"The 1D model is termed \"x-full\" (since it fully accounts for variation in "
"the x direction) and can be selected as follows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[7]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"options = {\"thermal\": \"x-full\"}\n"
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:314
msgid "Higher dimensional pouch cell models"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:316
msgid ""
"These pouch cell thermal models ignore any variation in temperature through "
"the thickness of the cell (x direction), and solve for :math:`T(y,z,t)`. It "
"is therefore referred to as an \"x-lumped\" model. The temperature is found "
"as the solution of a partial differential equation, given here in "
"dimensional terms,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:318
msgid ""
"\\rho_{eff} \\frac{\\partial T}{\\partial t} = \\lambda_{eff} "
"\\nabla_\\perp^2T + \\bar{Q} - \\frac{(h_{cn}+h_{cp})A}{V}(T-T_{\\infty}),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:323
msgid "along with boundary conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:325
msgid ""
"-\\lambda_{eff} \\nabla_\\perp T \\cdot \\boldsymbol{n} = \\frac{L_{cn}"
"h_{cn} + (L_n+L_s+L_p+L_{cp})h_{edge}}{L_{cn}+L_n+L_s+L_p+L_{cp}}(T-"
"T_\\infty),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:330
msgid "at the negative tab,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:332
msgid ""
"-\\lambda_{eff} \\nabla_\\perp T \\cdot \\boldsymbol{n} = "
"\\frac{(L_{cn}+L_n+L_s+L_p)h_{edge}+L_{cp}h_{cp}}{L_{cn}+L_n+L_s+L_p+L_{cp}}"
"(T-T_\\infty),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:337
msgid "at the positive tab, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:339
msgid ""
"-\\lambda_{eff} \\nabla_\\perp T \\cdot \\boldsymbol{n} = h_{edge}(T-"
"T_\\infty),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:344
msgid ""
"elsewhere. Again, an initial temperature :math:`T_0` must be prescribed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:346
msgid ""
"Here the heat source term is averaged in the x direction so that :math:"
"`\\bar{Q}=\\bar{Q}(y,z)`. The parameter :math:`\\lambda_{eff}` is the "
"effective thermal conductivity, computed as"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:348
msgid "\\lambda_{eff} = \\frac{\\sum_k \\lambda_k L_k}{\\sum_k L_k}."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:353
msgid ""
"The heat transfer coefficients :math:`h_{cn}`, :math:`h_{cp}` and :math:"
"`h_{egde}` correspond to heat transfer at the large surface of the pouch on "
"the side of the negative current collector, heat transfer at the large "
"surface of the pouch on the side of the positive current collector, and heat "
"transfer at the remaining, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:357
msgid "The \"2+1D\" model can be selected as follows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[8]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"options = {\n"
"    \"current collector\": \"potential pair\",\n"
"    \"dimensionality\": 2,\n"
"    \"thermal\": \"x-lumped\",\n"
"}\n"
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN(options)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:384
msgid "Model usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:395
msgid ""
"Here we compare the \"full\" one-dimensional model with the lumped model for "
"a pouch cell. We first set up our models, passing the relevant options, and "
"then show how to adjust the parameters to so that the lumped and full models "
"give the same behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[9]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"full_thermal_model = pybamm.lithium_ion.SPMe(\n"
"    {\"thermal\": \"x-full\"}, name=\"full thermal model\"\n"
")\n"
"lumped_thermal_model = pybamm.lithium_ion.SPMe(\n"
"    {\"thermal\": \"lumped\"}, name=\"lumped thermal model\"\n"
")\n"
"models = [full_thermal_model, lumped_thermal_model]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:422
msgid "We then pick our parameter set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[10]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "parameter_values = pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Marquis2019\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:443
msgid ""
"For the \"full\" model we use a heat transfer coefficient of :math:`5\\,  "
"\\text{Wm}^{-2}\\text{K}^{-1}` on the large surfaces of the pouch and zero "
"heat transfer coefficient on the tabs and edges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[11]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"full_params = parameter_values.copy()\n"
"full_params.update(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"Negative current collector\"\n"
"        + \" surface heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 5,\n"
"        \"Positive current collector\"\n"
"        + \" surface heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 5,\n"
"        \"Negative tab heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 0,\n"
"        \"Positive tab heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 0,\n"
"        \"Edge heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 0,\n"
"    }\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:475
msgid ""
"For the lumped model we set the \"Total heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2."
"K-1]\" parameter as well as the \"Cell cooling surface area [m2]\" "
"parameter. Since the \"full\" model only accounts for cooling from the large "
"surfaces of the pouch, we set the \"Surface area for cooling\" parameter to "
"the area of the large surfaces of the pouch, and the total heat transfer "
"coefficient to :math:`5\\,  \\text{Wm}^{-2}\\text{K}^{-1}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[12]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"A = parameter_values[\"Electrode width [m]\"] * parameter_values[\"Electrode "
"height [m]\"]\n"
"lumped_params = parameter_values.copy()\n"
"lumped_params.update(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"Total heat transfer coefficient [W.m-2.K-1]\": 5,\n"
"        \"Cell cooling surface area [m2]\": 2 * A,\n"
"    }\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:503
msgid ""
"Let's run simulations with both options and compare the results. For "
"demonstration purposes we'll increase the current to amplify the thermal "
"effects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid "[13]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"params = [full_params, lumped_params]\n"
"# loop over the models and solve\n"
"sols = []\n"
"for model, param in zip(models, params, strict=False):\n"
"    param[\"Current function [A]\"] = 3 * 0.68\n"
"    sim = pybamm.Simulation(model, parameter_values=param)\n"
"    sim.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"    sols.append(sim.solution)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"# plot\n"
"output_variables = [\n"
"    \"Voltage [V]\",\n"
"    \"X-averaged cell temperature [K]\",\n"
"    \"Cell temperature [K]\",\n"
"]\n"
"pybamm.dynamic_plot(sols, output_variables)\n"
"\n"
"# plot the results\n"
"pybamm.dynamic_plot(\n"
"    sols,\n"
"    [\n"
"        \"Volume-averaged cell temperature [K]\",\n"
"        \"Volume-averaged total heating [W.m-3]\",\n"
"        \"Current [A]\",\n"
"        \"Voltage [V]\",\n"
"    ],\n"
")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/thermal-models.ipynb:553
msgid ""
"<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">{\"model_id\": "
"\"b29f3527b0cb47b888bf748ff800f359\", \"version_major\": 2, "
